{"text": "Castellano & Reyes Criminal Defense, Ltd.\nPRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL -- ATTORNEY-CLIENT COMMUNICATION / WORK PRODUCT\nTo: Benedikt Reyes\nFrom: Rhiannon Castellano\nDate: September 29, 2026\nRe: New client intake -- State v. Ibarra-Lund, Case No. CR26-1447\nClient\nField\tDetail\nName\tIBARRA-LUND, MATEO\nAlso known as\t\"Teo\"\nDate of birth\t06/27/1996\nSSN\t493211306\nNevada DL\t1702884415\nBooking no.\t26-0091873\nStatus\tlawful permanent resident\nHome\t2290 Wedekind Road, Apt. 14\nCity\tSparks, NV 89431\nPhone\t775-555-0148 (phone seized)\nMother\tLucia Ibarra, 775-555-0115\n\nCharges and custody\nMateo Ibarra-Lund was arrested on Sept. 24, 2026 after a traffic stop on Pyramid Way. He is charged with possession of a controlled substance for sale (NRS 453.337, a Category B felony) and possession of a firearm by a prohibited person (NRS 202.360). Bail was set at $25,000 by Judge Egon Pruett in Department 4. His mother posted through High Desert Bail Bonds and paid a premium of $3,750; she put up the title to her car. He was released the evening of 9/26/26. Arraignment is set for October 14, 2026.\nWhat he says happened\nHe was driving his girlfriend's car, a 2019 Honda Accord, VIN 1HGCV1F32KU724601, Nevada plate 448-LRT. The girlfriend is Kaylee Voss. Detective Cole Brannigan says he smelled marijuana and searched the trunk, where he found a backpack with about 61 grams of methamphetamine and a 9 mm pistol, serial number BKRT417. Teo says the backpack belongs to Kaylee's cousin, Travis Oyelaran (\"Tre\"), who had borrowed the car that weekend. He did not consent to the search. He says he asked for a lawyer twice before Brannigan kept questioning him; if that holds up we have a Miranda issue.\nPolice also seized his phone, IMEI 356938112047755, and have applied for a warrant. He gave them the passcode (271996) at the roadside. He thinks there are messages with Tre on a marketplace account under the username teo_lund96.\nRecord and exposure\nHe has a 2017 felony conviction for burglary in Washoe County, case CR17-0832, for which he served 14 months. That prior is what makes the gun charge possible. Because he is not a U.S. citizen, a drug-sale conviction almost certainly means removal. He was brought from Sinaloa at age four and has no family there. We need a Padilla advisal in writing before any plea discussion.\nPersonal circumstances\nHe has worked for Sierra Crest Roofing & Gutter LLC since 2022 at $27 an hour; his foreman will write a letter. He reports daily methamphetamine use until last spring and six months sober since entering an outpatient program. He takes buprenorphine and is worried about missing doses if he is taken back into custody. Ms. Voss is five months pregnant.\nFee\nFlat fee through preliminary hearing: $8,500. His mother paid $2,000 by card today (Visa ending 8293, exp. 04/29). The balance is due in four payments.\nTo do\nBen: request body-camera video and the dispatch log today.\nSubpoena Sierra Crest time sheets for the weekend before the arrest.\nInterview Ms. Voss separately; she may need her own lawyer.\n-- RC", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "504 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Benedikt Reyes", "IBARRA-LUND, MATEO", "Lucia Ibarra", "Mateo Ibarra-Lund", "Kaylee Voss", "Travis Oyelaran", "Cole Brannigan", "Egon Pruett", "Ben", "Ms. Voss"], "companies": ["Castellano & Reyes Criminal Defense, Ltd.", "Sierra Crest Roofing & Gutter LLC", "High Desert Bail Bonds"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.8999999985098839, "modelMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 41, "text": "Castellano & Reyes Criminal Defense, Ltd.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Castellano & Reyes Crimi